# The sample platformer: players are characters running and jumping about a
# level of platforms and slopes and shooting at each other, where the shooter
# saw the others; a runner hit is told so and counts it. Everything a player does moves no dynamic body, so a client
# predicts its own runner exactly; each client is sent what is within 30
# meters and sees the others between states.
program runners.kest
physics2d gravity 0 -10 substeps 4

collision class runner 2ebcd16c10c5f6a4

# Split-screen (D364): two local players one over the other, four in
# quarters.
layout 2 0 0 1 0.5 0 0.5 1 0.5
layout 4 0 0 0.5 0.5 0.5 0 0.5 0.5 0 0.5 0.5 0.5 0.5 0.5 0.5 0.5
# Every player sees the level in 16:9, however the window or its region is
# shaped, between slate bars (D369): no shape of window shows more of it.
aspect 16 9 24 28 40

component 6b05cdb4-0683-437a-aaac-7ad990b2ddb4 runners.stick Stick
component f6453556-fcdd-46e8-9208-866fade389cf runners.score Score
component 4a1a3d29-28e9-46fe-aae0-6bb3576ca9b3 runners.hit Hit
component 5f3691c6-292c-4054-b868-142fe8a4448f runners.emitter Emitter
component 8c4e2a17-5b90-4d3f-a6e8-1f7c9d0b2e53 runners.age Age
# No entity holds a penalty: it is what the penalty service is asked about.
component 3d8b6f21-7c4e-4a95-b0d3-e6f1a2c95b78 runners.penalty Penalty
component 1e7c5a93-4f28-4b6d-8a01-c3d9e2f4b7a5 runners.look rawframe.canvas.Sprite
component 9d3e61b2-7a4c-4f05-b8e1-2c6a0f9d4b37 runners.tile rawframe.canvas.Sprite
component 3149b7ac-718f-4686-a572-6241d54af2a3 runners.view rawframe.canvas.Camera
component b668075a-c5b2-45fa-af7e-0aa7f62c8808 runners.wince rawframe.sound.Emitter
component c68ee156-5575-4b58-9ed0-41395d2a7bdc runners.dust rawframe.model.Trail
component fd2777e2-c81b-4588-9117-dd0e4acc564d runners.sparks rawframe.model.ParticleEmitter
component d30c12f9-2754-4113-9519-0afbf0ea2970 runners.hud rawframe.ui.Node
component 6293ab03-1010-42b8-bef6-f06379468d19 runners.landed rawframe.ui.Node
component 1e5be856-5be3-47ab-84a3-433ac63f84c6 runners.taken rawframe.ui.Node

system runners.join simulation join write rawframe.physics2d.body write rawframe.physics2d.pose write rawframe.physics2d.character with runners.stick random spawn before rawframe.physics2d.step
system runners.run simulation run read runners.stick read rawframe.physics2d.character write rawframe.physics2d.velocity entities before rawframe.physics2d.step predicted emits jump
system runners.shoot simulation shoot read runners.stick read rawframe.physics2d.pose read rawframe.replication.perception write runners.score write runners.emitter before rawframe.physics2d.step
system runners.hurt simulation hurt write runners.score read runners.hit entities
system runners.age simulation age write runners.age

# A jump is a presentation effect the runner predicts: its player hears it
# at once, and once (D219), as jump.sound (D220), and feels it on a gamepad
# as a short, low thump (D251).
effect jump predicted sound 57164ad59d5b6a23 felt thump 0.4 60 90

# The level (level.scene): the ground, eighty meters wide, walls at its
# ends, three platforms to jump up to, slopes of 20 degrees at both ends,
# and one of 55 too steep to stand on.
scene level.scene

# The hall (hall.scene): one persistent entity that keeps how long the level
# has been played. A server with `save.directory` keeps it between runs.
scene hall.scene
save hall runners.age
# Each player keeps their score between visits, under the session they ask
# for.
save player runner runners.score

# Anyone may mod it. A mod adds timers, entities holding runners.age that the
# age system counts up as it does the hall's (runners-timers is one), and
# handles hits: right after hurt, over each runner hit, it may change the
# runner's score (runners-sting is one). One mod may also say what a hit
# costs: hurt asks the penalty service, which answers one taken unless a
# mod provides it (runners-penalty is one). And one mod may replace how the
# hall and every timer age (runners-swift is one).
mods open
modapi runners 1
extension timers data runners.age multi
extension hits event runners.hit after runners.hurt write runners.score multi
extension penalty service runners.penalty exclusive
# When more than one mod provides the penalty, runners-penalty's is kept and
# the others' are set aside.
prefer penalty rawframe/runners-penalty
extension aging replacement runners.age exclusive

replicate rawframe.physics2d.body rawframe.physics2d.pose rawframe.physics2d.velocity rawframe.physics2d.character runners.stick runners.score runners.emitter runners.tile
player runners.stick runners.score runners.emitter rawframe.physics2d.body rawframe.physics2d.pose rawframe.physics2d.velocity rawframe.physics2d.character rawframe.replication.perception
input runners.stick perceived
# A client makes its stick from its player's actions (runners.actions) with
# sample.kest; bots press the same keys and buttons.
actions runners.actions
sample sample.kest sample
interest rawframe.physics2d.pose x y within 30
interpolate rawframe.physics2d.pose
predict rawframe.physics2d.body rawframe.physics2d.pose rawframe.physics2d.velocity rawframe.physics2d.character runners.stick

# Each shot sounds from the runner that fired it (runners.mixer, shot.sound);
# clients hear them, a server carries only the counts. A jump sounds from
# the runner that jumped, heard by its own player only. A hit runner's
# player hears it wince (hurt.sound) from an emitter of its client's own
# (D272), cued when the server tells of the hit.
mixer runners.mixer
sound 950e09337d03de69 shot.sound
sound 57164ad59d5b6a23 jump.sound
sound 81012dde2ad3952f hurt.sound

# What a client shows: the HUD's words in English and Turkish (hud.strings,
# hud.tr.translations), English unless the player asks otherwise. A server
# never reads them.
text hud.strings
text hud.tr.translations
locale en

# What a client draws (D254): runners (runner.png) over the level's tiles
# (tiles.png, the level's runners.tile), through its own runner's camera
# (D261), 12 meters tall and leading the way it runs. A runner's look is the client's own (D260): each
# client gives every runner it mirrors a look and an animator
# (runner.rfanim) that steps its sheet's frame from its stick, standing,
# running, or in the air (D258); no server carries or sends them.
animator 4b1c7e29a05d3f86 runner.rfanim parameters runners.stick
presentation runners.look rawframe.animation.animator on runners.stick
present runners.dress dress read runners.stick write runners.look write rawframe.animation.animator
presentation runners.view on player
message hurt Hurt
present runners.frame frame read runners.stick write runners.view
presentation runners.wince on player
present runners.wince wince write runners.wince
# Every runner a client mirrors leaves a pale trail as it runs, and throws
# sparks with each shot it fires, counted by its shot's cue (D357): the
# client's own particles, drawn over the canvas.
presentation runners.dust runners.sparks on runners.stick
present runners.glint glint read runners.emitter write runners.dust write runners.sparks
# The player's HUD (D376): a panel along the bottom of its view, a green
# meter of the hits its runner landed and a red one of those it took, each
# filling over ten and starting again; the client's own, drawn over all.
presentation runners.hud runners.landed runners.taken on player
ui runners.landed in runners.hud
ui runners.taken in runners.hud
present runners.gauge gauge read runners.score write runners.hud write runners.landed write runners.taken
texture eddbc014cab63eb2 runner.png
texture a44ecb4a39ac5cc8 tiles.png
# The runners' look lit a little warm from within: a canvas material
# (D356).
material ea61c563796c6e4b runner.rfmaterial
